,"type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2014-03-12T04:28:13Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/37420913","html_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/2297#issuecomment-37420913","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/2297","id":37420913,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NDIwOTEz","user":{"login":"opinali","id":3017776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTc3NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3017776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali","html_url":"https://github.com/opinali","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-03-12T15:21:13Z","updated_at":"2014-03-12T15:21:13Z","body":"Well, I looked at the maven logs now and it's obviously a platform issue. Building on Google corp machines, which have tons of custom network/security configuration. On OSX, which I was using before, there's a failure resolving the local host's canonical domain name; this had already happened to me in my own Java projects. Now on my Ubuntu PC, I have a different error, also network-related and maybe more important:\n\nTests run: 4, Failures: 0, Errors: 1, Skipped: 0, Time elapsed: 0.733 sec <<< FAILURE! - in io.netty.handler.ipfilter.IpSubnetFilterTest\ntestIpFilterRuleHandler(io.netty.handler.ipfilter.IpSubnetFilterTest)  Time elapsed: 0.683 sec  <<< ERROR!\njava.lang.NullPointerException: null\n    at io.netty.handler.ipfilter.IpSubnetFilterTest.testIpFilterRuleHandler(IpSubnetFilterTest.java:86)\n\nHere it seems the test is opening channels to private network addresses (192.168.*) and this fails, so readOutbound() == null, so the registration should be failing for some reason; I didn't investigate deeply but it's a safe guess the test is making some assumption that doesn't work in my network.\n\nI just disabled testIpFilterRuleHandler to move forward, then next failure was installing a plugin:\n\nDownloaded: http://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/org/fusesource/hawtjni/hawtjni-generator/1.10/hawtjni-generator-1.10.jar (377 KB at 20941.1 KB/sec)\n[INFO] executing: /bin/sh -c ./autogen.sh\n[INFO] auto reconf...\n[INFO] ./autogen.sh: line 33: autoreconf: command not found\n[INFO] rc: 127\n[INFO] \n\nI found out that this required the package dh-autoreconf; may be worth pointing that need in CONTRIBUTING.md since it's not a standard package at least on Ubuntu 12.04.\n\nAfter a successful build, I was able to test my code with the closeFuture().sync() and now everything worked, so this bug is fix for me. Changing the testIpFilterRuleHandler test to be more \"portable\", or lenient with network failures, would be nice though.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/37420913/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"opinali","id":3017776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTc3NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3017776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/opinali","html_url":"https://github.com/opinali","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/opin